{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1506251-is-it-a-good-idea-to-play-each-other-s-geister-like-shadows-in-wraith","id":1506251,"title":"Is it a good idea to play each other's Geister, like Shadows in Wraith?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-23T11:30:10-07:00","id":1506251,"title":"Is it a good idea to play each other's Geister, like Shadows in Wraith?","content":"Disclaimer: I am not too familiar with Geist nor Wraith, though I do recall that Shadows are inherently antagonistic and mean-spirited, but Geister are not. How would the variable nature of personalities among Geister affect such a dynamic between players? Could it generate enough meaningful drama and conflict to be its own recurring source of Beats?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T15:24:22-07:00","id":1506270,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I got called to dinner as soon as I saw you post, so I was a little curt.<br /> <br /> Short answer is no. Longer answer is that Geists should be the opposite of Shadows, in almost every way. They made a Bargain with someone to stay in the Mortal world and to affect it. They need the Sin Eater to do something, and in the best case scenario (for the Geist) the Sin Eater they bargain with should have a need to do the same thing as well. <br /> <br /> I'm not trying to say that Geists and Sin Eaters should always get along. They are two different individuals, one of which has become very alien, both to their Mortal world and the Sin Eater anchoring them to it. But, at least up to a point, Geists and their Sin Eaters should have a common purpose, and want each other to succeed.<br /> <br /> Hope this helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3201,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","user":"Father Enoch","date":". 03-23-2023, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T17:40:12-07:00","id":1506277,"title":"","content":"I would say no. One important thing about the Shadow and why it is played by another player is that it can tempt the wraith with offers of power, while wanting the wraith to fail at everything. That means it can offer, or withhold, power at times that a single player probably wouldn't do. <br /> <br /> That's not true of a Geist. It doesn't have a reason to be rooting against it's Sin Eater nor does it have dark power it can tempt people with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T20:36:27-07:00","id":1506286,"title":"","content":"Okay, well, to be a point of dissent: Geists are still distinct enough characters with an evolving relationship that goes from hostile (on account of not really being successful with any social rolls except for Intimidation and not knowing each other) to sympathetic(&quot;No, don't worry about them, I know what they mean and it's not that&quot;) that allowing another player to roleplay as a character's Geist is not only viable but possibly very fun, and emphasizes the ways in which a Geist and a Sin-Eater can both agree and disagree.<br /> <br /> as of beats, eh, maybe? A lot of the situations where that would apply already applied to Beats, it's just making the actual moment of earning them more dynamic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-23T21:23:15-07:00","id":1506289,"title":"","content":"The answer to the question in the title <i>without</i> the comma is &quot;absolutely not.&quot; Geists exist independently of the Bargain and the ones that don't care to play the long game corrupting one of the Bound into fulfilling hypothetical dark urges behind their Remembrance have better tools for that job than forsaking most of their capacity for independent action in favor of a give-and-take relationship. Geists are cryptic and spooky, but most of the ones who offer the Bargain aren't grappling for control of your body or trying to get you to give into your darker impulses (as the Tyrannous demonstrate, <i>you</i> are the primary risk on that front.)<br /> <br /> As for the question as-written, it's about as good an idea as having players who aren't in the Storyteller's role for the story/chronicle play any other NPC \u2014 it will vary substantially by table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T07:22:39-08:00","id":1526924,"title":"","content":"It depends on your players. Geists had a reason to offer the Bargain, they also stand to benefit from it. Some of their memories might have been lost from either spending years in the Underworld, and they certainly lost some when drinking from a River.<br /> <br /> The Geist doesn't necessarily have a reason to sabotage the Sin Eeater. They are also getting used to the other person they are sharing an existence with. There might be issues if they do not resonate with each other's goals (like a former mobster Geist wanting to eliminate the descendants of his killers), which may lead to manipulation, but the Sin Eater being emotionally broken or dieying constantly is just bad for both of them.<br /> <br /> If that sounds interesting to your players and they can handle the rough outlines of the Geist's memories without using them to metagame, then go for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T12:43:23-08:00","id":1526993,"title":"","content":"Is it a good idea? That depends on whether it was a good idea in Wraith, and whether that can be used to make Geist better.<br /> <br /> Alas, all I know it that Wraith has been described as too difficult to play, which leads me to think maybe it didn't work well in Wraith. But I am more than happy to be convinced that this one mechanic would make Geist better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-17T14:07:04-08:00","id":1527001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1506251-is-it-a-good-idea-to-play-each-other-s-geister-like-shadows-in-wraith?p=1526993#post1526993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it a good idea? That depends on whether it was a good idea in Wraith, and whether that can be used to make Geist better.<br /> <br /> Alas, all I know it that Wraith has been described as too difficult to play, which leads me to think maybe it didn't work well in Wraith. But I am more than happy to be convinced that this one mechanic would make Geist better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a big fan of wraith, as a setting but I do agree it has difficulties. Its difficulties do not come from the playing one another's shadows. <br /> <br /> That said, as I said, I don't think it's a good idea. It's mechanically a part of wraith, the shadows have abilities, they have goals that they can work toward in a number of ways. Geist's have very limited mechanics, sketchy goals they can't accomplish without their sin eater, and sometimes barely any understanding of who or what they are <br /> <br /> But it isn't *just* that. Shadows are an omnipresent part of wraith, a shadow can offer it's wraith powers, bonus dice, and tons of things (depending upon the build) that the wraith doesn't have access to by themselves. It would be a lot to remember as a storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-08T07:35:44-07:00","id":1533815,"title":"","content":"While it definitely can be done, and I\u2019ve seen it done well.. it\u2019s really something you should only suggest to a very close knit and experienced table. Better to have the storyteller portray thr Geister than players who might go a tad bit too far.<br /> <br /> That said, I do kinda take exception to the idea of comparing a Geist to a Shadow. The Geist isn\u2019t your darkest impulses given sapience and a desire to utterly undermine and destroy you as insidiously as it possibly can. A Geist is a broken being that has a measure of darkly divine power, but the cost of that power is coherence and emotional instability. I also firmly prescribe to the idea that while they desire and act on things that can be very difficult to comprehend for their human partner.. most Geister aren\u2019t intrinsically opposed to the Bound in all things like a Shadow. They might have very different intentions than their human half, but that serves to help bridge a gap and help the two gradually come to understand each other. This makes it attractive to see if your players can pull off such complex interpersonal discourse\u2026 but it\u2019s a fine line to walk on.<br /> <br /> So my input is : If you think your table can handle it, give it a try. If not? Well there are plenty of alternatives when it comes to portray Geister that are much more palatable to troupe play.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}